{
	title: 'Subagents report back by themselves; spawn starts fresh',
	description: "A subagent's answer reaches its parent without the send tool: when a turn of a subagent-kind session that its parent started (the first task, or a later message from the parent) ends, the host delivers the turn's last assistant text to the parent as a message from the child, advisory like any agent message. A turn that ends with no assistant text still reports: 'Session <label> finished without a message'; one that ends failed or paused says so and why ('Session <label> stopped: <reason>'), so a parent never waits for a child that has stopped. The child's first prompt no longer tells it to send a handoff; it says its last message is returned to the parent. Turns the user starts in a promoted (left-open) subagent report nothing. spawn's mode defaults to fresh for every kind (questions: user's answers of 27 Sep): a subagent gets clear guidance in its task instead of the parent's context; fork stays available on request. Messages from other sessions to a session the user paused wait until he continues it (as task rj built).",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['t0'],
	foldInto: ['t0']
}
